-- What can this instance reach?
--
--   drt run --config auditor.json
--   drt run --config worker.json
--   drt run --config ungranted.json
--
-- One call answers it. The same program runs under all three configs; every
-- difference in the output is the deployment's doing.

-- The menu is a list of tables, one per connector family this process wired,
-- plus an entry for the menu itself. `granted` is asked the way a call asks:
-- it is what THIS instance may reach, not what the process carries.
--
-- example: omits host.try — a program allowed to ask this is a program that
-- should stop if the answer is refused, so the raising form is the right one
for _, entry in ipairs(host.call("capabilities/list")) do
    print(string.format("  %-12s %-8s granted=%s", entry.name, entry.kind, tostring(entry.granted)))
end
